  "risk_rating": "critical",
  "short_description": "The Google Brotli decoder between 1.0.3 and 1.2.0 misreports an invalid block switch as a temporary need for more input and keeps appending bytes to an eight-byte internal buffer, writing out of bounds (CVE-2026-111497, CVSS 9.8, tracked as Node2Shell); anything that decompresses attacker-controlled Brotli streams — web servers and runtimes accepting Content-Encoding: br request bodies, Node.js, .NET, and embedded copies in Go, Python, Rust and mobile native libraries — must move to 1.0.10 / 1.1.1 / 1.2.1 (or the fixed runtime).",
